                            <comment id="495049" author="yujian" created="Tue, 26 May 2026 18:52:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The failure occurred 169 times in the past 2 weeks.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="497377" author="adilger" created="Tue, 7 Jul 2026 12:17:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+49 failures last week:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=4f25830c-64fe-11e2-bfb2-52540035b04c&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=4f398866-64fe-11e2-bfb2-52540035b04c&amp;amp;start_date=2026-07-01&amp;amp;end_date=2026-07-07&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=4f25830c-64fe-11e2-bfb2-52540035b04c&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=4f398866-64fe-11e2-bfb2-52540035b04c&amp;amp;start_date=2026-07-01&amp;amp;end_date=2026-07-07&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="497378" author="adilger" created="Tue, 7 Jul 2026 12:29:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This subtest is running LFSCK on a newly-formatted filesystem with some files created in it, so it is surprising to have it repair anything.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It seems to only be failing on el10.1 servers. It fails 100% with ldiskfs, and never with zfs. . &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="497379" author="adilger" created="Tue, 7 Jul 2026 13:01:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ablagodarenko&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ablagodarenko&quot;&gt;ablagodarenko&lt;/a&gt; it looks like this failure (and many others in sanity-lfsck, test_1a, test_1b, ...) are caused by the revised dirdata series which landed on 2026-05-29 when this first started failing on el10.0, and then moved to el10.1 when that started testing. There were also failures on master-next the previous week before that patch was landed, but they were missed.  The sanity-lfsck sessions are failing 100% of runs, so it should be straight forward to determine what is going wrong. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="497407" author="JIRAUSER18021" created="Tue, 7 Jul 2026 19:48:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It looks like the root cause is the same as &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20424&quot; title=&quot;osd_fid_unpack() unexpected packed fid size: 0&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20424&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20424&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I see in logs a lot of such messages&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
./sanity-lfsck.test_38.debug_log.trevis-153vm243.1775255053.log:00080000:00020000:0.0:1775255015.017654:0:564853:0:(osd_internal.h:1534:osd_fid_unpack()) unexpected packed fid size: 0
./sanity-lfsck.test_38.debug_log.trevis-153vm243.1775255053.log:00080000:00020000:0.0:1775255015.017655:0:564853:0:(osd_internal.h:1534:osd_fid_unpack()) unexpected packed fid size: 0 &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=bzzz&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;bzzz&quot;&gt;bzzz&lt;/a&gt; provided a fix and sanity-lfsck almost passes on RHEL 10.1 with 6.12.0-124.56.1_lustre.el10.x86_64 kernel. Some of tests fail, but it looks for some other reasons, not this issue &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/f6c05499-b19d-4896-8d04-ce1d8cd83f00&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/f6c05499-b19d-4896-8d04-ce1d8cd83f00&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="498476" author="JIRAUSER18021" created="Fri, 24 Jul 2026 09:52:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20424&quot; title=&quot;osd_fid_unpack() unexpected packed fid size: 0&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20424&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20424&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; solution is landed now&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
